	abstract = {Prognostics and health management ({PHM}) facilitates maintenance decision-making and provides usage feedback for the product design and validation process. Electronic component and product manufacturers need new ways to gain insights from the massive volume of data recently streaming in from their systems and sensors, and this can be accomplished by using machine learning ({ML}). This chapter provides the fundamentals of {ML}. {ML} algorithms can be divided into the following four categories depending on the amount and type of supervision they need while training: supervised, unsupervised, semi-supervised, and reinforcement learning. {ML} algorithms can be classified into two different learning methods based on whether or not the algorithms can learn incrementally from a stream of incoming data: batch and online learning. Probability theory plays a significant role in {ML}, specifically as the design of learning algorithms often depends on probabilistic assumption of the data.},
